{"approach":"I followed the DE-04 procedure in the data-engineering-steps skill. First I read the four contracted inputs: feat.tasks, feat.design, org.data_model and task.repo_access. Then I read the existing ap_pipeline sources and pipelines: the tool view of ingest, transform, dq, pipeline, schedule.json, __init__ and the tests, plus ci.py and data/sample_feed.csv, which I opened with Read and Glob. The G9 hook blocks shell commands in this step.

I took background from journey:feat.clarifications (the CL-DE answers) and journey:task.db_changes, both read through context_get with receipts. For secrets in all environments I used the approved DE-02 task.secrets_scope file. I classified each existing element by layer and chose the smallest change set. There is no new source or pipeline, and parse_feed is unchanged because it is header-driven. The optional column is let in with an additive update to transform.to_model (TSK-01). The new delays.py (TSK-02) is listed and left to DE-07 for detail.

The output file already held a stale DE-07 version from an earlier run, and I overwrote it with the DE-04 content. A verifier subagent then checked the draft. It found three issues, which I fixed: the source for "empty when unpaid" is now record:memory, the line about CI and tests is now labelled as agent judgement, and I added the context_list citation for the input commits. No connectors were needed.","tools_used":["Skill (data-engineering-steps)","Read","Glob","mcp__hobasa-context__context_list","mcp__hobasa-context__context_get (feat.clarifications, task.db_changes)","mcp__hobasa-context__memory_search","Agent (verifier)","Write","Edit"],"claims":[{"text":"The ingestion entry point parse_feed uses csv.DictReader over io.StringIO and returns one dict per row keyed by the header. It reads no column by name, so a v3 paid_date column passes through without a code change.","source":"tool:repo"},{"text":"transform.to_model today builds id, vendor, due_date, amount and paid inside one try block. It rejects rows on KeyError, ValueError, InvalidOperation or AttributeError, using the exception type name as the reason.","source":"tool:repo"},{"text":"The minimum ingestion-side change is an additive update to to_model. It adds PAID_DATE_REASON and _parse_paid_date, and parses paid_date only after the existing try succeeds, so an invalid value is rejected with reason 'paid_date' rather than 'ValueError'.","source":"feat.design; feat.tasks; journey:feat.clarifications"},{"text":"ingest.py, dq.py, pipeline.py and schedule.json are on TSK-01's 'Must not change' list, and the design marks parse_feed, quality_report and run as unchanged (HC-3).","source":"feat.tasks; feat.design"},{"text":"TSK-02 creates the new module src/ap_pipeline/delays.py with delays_by_vendor, a pure function that returns Dict[str, List[int]] from paid records that have a paid_date.","source":"feat.tasks; feat.design"},{"text":"The schedule stays daily at 02:00 Asia/Kolkata.","source":"tool:repo; feat.design"},{"text":"The checked-in sample feed has the v2 header invoice_id,vendor,due_date,amount,paid, with no paid_date column.","source":"file:ap_pipeline/data/sample_feed.csv"},{"text":"The registered Invoice model has paid_date as date or None, added in feed v3.","source":"org.data_model"},{"text":"The ap_pipeline version is 0.4.0, and TSK-01 owns the version step.","source":"task.repo_access; feat.tasks"},{"text":"No secret is required or granted for ap_pipeline in development, integration (dev) or production (main), so there is no gap.","source":"file:hobasa-data-engineering-agent/outputs/FEAT-ZD-48600/task.secrets_scope.md"},{"text":"No database change is needed, and the design adds no storage, service or library.","source":"journey:task.db_changes; feat.design"},{"text":"CI requires coverage of at least 90.0 and runs static checks for print, eval, exec, bare except and lines over 140 characters.","source":"file:ap_pipeline/ci.py"},{"text":"Feed v3 in production (PQ-6) gates release, not coding; the lane builds on synthetic v3 rows.","source":"feat.tasks; feat.design; journey:feat.clarifications"},{"text":"The requirement states that paid_date is an optional ISO date column that is empty when unpaid.","source":"record:memory"}],"open_questions":["CQ-I1: Is the v3 header spelled exactly 'paid_date'? parse_feed matches header text exactly, so a different spelling would load silently as paid_date = None. Interim answer: yes, as in org.data_model. Owner: Data engineering lead / feed owner.","CQ-I2 (carried DQ-1): Which production component fetches the feed and calls pipeline.run and delays_by_vendor? Interim answer: only the end-to-end harness wires the stages in this feature. Owner: Architect.","CQ-I3 (carried OQ-B6): Should an unpaid row that has a paid_date be rejected? Interim answer: it is accepted and the date is kept (DD-7). Owner: Product / Architect.","CQ-I4: Should data/sample_feed.csv gain a v3 example? It is outside the task file budgets. Interim answer: no change. Owner: Data engineering lead."],"summary":"I wrote task.components for DE-04. Result: the ingestion layer needs no code change and there is no new source or pipeline. The vendor CSV feed stays the only source, and the header-driven parse_feed already carries the optional v3 paid_date column. The minimum change set is:
- an additive update to transform.to_model (TSK-01), which parses paid_date after the existing try and rejects an invalid value with reason 'paid_date';
- one new pure module, delays.py (TSK-02), which DE-07 details.

dq.quality_report, pipeline.run, schedule.json (daily 02:00 Asia/Kolkata) and the v2 sample feed stay as they are. No secret is required or granted in development, integration or production. The file also lists the file budget, the must-not-change files, risks, the hand-off to DE-05, DE-07 and DE-08, and four non-blocking open questions; the main one is the exact spelling of the v3 header. A stale DE-07 version of the output file from an earlier run was overwritten. There are no blocking questions."}
